      "widgets_values": [
        "A candid, low-angle DSLR photograph captured with a Nikon D850 and an ultra-wide 14mm f/1.8 lens, shot from a true worm's-eye view at ground level, pointing sharply upward.\n\nThe optical focus is razor-sharp on the weathered, cracked human skull resting in the immediate foreground, creating an extremely shallow depth of field. Every micro-crack, bone texture, and speck of dirt on the skull is crisp, while the demon woman's towering figure directly behind it falls into a soft, creamy background bokeh beneath a vast, vibrant blue sky.\n\nThe demon woman stands turned in profile, her left leg lifted so that her left boot rests firmly on top of the skull with her left knee bent at a sharp angle. Her right leg remains straight to anchor her weight, creating a dynamic, dominant stance. The dramatic wide-angle forced perspective makes the skull appear massive in the foreground while exaggerating her monumental height overhead. The wind blows her cloak slightly to the side, revealing her athletic body. Natural, harsh midday sun casts crisp shadows across the gritty ground, featuring subtle chromatic aberration, fine sensor noise, and a flat, desaturated color grade. RAW photo, un-retouched."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
